    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῡσ-ωπός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤψ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with golden eyes</i> or <i>face, beaming like
			gold,</i> of the sun, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				740
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Corn.
				<u>ND</u>
				32
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					[1128]
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>gold-coloured,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάργαρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					15.8
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a fish, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρύσοφρυς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.977f
			</span></i>.</div>
